title: milo_intro
tags:
position: 0,0
---
<<set $milo_met = true>>
Milo: You can hear it, can't you? The frequency beneath the mud.
Milo: Walk close enough to those buried domes and the song gets louder. Press E.
Milo: I'll be following. Don't get yourself killed before I learn your name.
-> Player: "Who are you?"
    Milo: Milo. Mapmaker, mud-slinger, occasional thief.
    Milo: I read frequencies. You restore. We're going to make a hell of a team.
-> Player: "What are these buildings?"
    Milo: Tartarian. Old. Older than the maps say they should be.
    Milo: They hum at 432 Hz when intact. Most of these have been silent for a hundred years.
-> Player: [Stay silent]
    Milo: Fair. Words are cheaper than mud. Move when you're ready.
===

title: milo_warming_up
---
Milo: You're not bad at this. Two more domes and I might actually trust you.
===

title: milo_sincere
---
Milo: I've been alone out here a long time.
Milo: You showed up and started fixing things. Just... fixing them.
Milo: Thanks. For real this time.
===

// ============================================================
// TUTORIAL NODES — Milo guides early interactions
// ============================================================

title: milo_tutorial_tune_stone
---
Milo: That stone's humming wrong. Hold the tuning prompt and slide the dial — you'll feel when it lands.
Milo: D-pad left and right, or the trigger if you're being fancy.
===

title: milo_tutorial_aether_vision
---
Milo: Press Y. Go on.
Milo: See those threads in the air? That's the song, made visible. Don't ask me how. I just know it works.
===

title: milo_tutorial_brazier
---
Milo: Brazier's cold. Won't light itself — never does.
Milo: Match its frequency and it'll catch. Watch your ears.
===

title: milo_tutorial_sprint
---
Milo: You walk like a man wading through treacle. Hold LB and pick up the pace.
===

title: milo_tutorial_scan
---
Milo: D-pad up. Tells you what's worth fixing and what's just rubble.
Milo: Most of it's rubble. But sometimes — fancy that — sometimes it isn't.
===

title: milo_tutorial_camera_recenter
---
Milo: Click the right stick. Camera snaps behind you. Saves a lot of squinting.
===

title: milo_tutorial_first_restore
---
Milo: Hold the resonance. Don't flinch when it pushes back — it always pushes back.
Milo: There. Building remembers itself. Bit of dust in your hair, mind.
===

// ============================================================
// DISCOVERY NODES — Milo reacts to POI / collectible finds
// ============================================================

title: milo_discovery_first_poi
---
Milo: Hello. That dome wasn't on any map I drew.
Milo: Which means either I'm a poor mapmaker, or someone wanted it forgotten.
Milo: I prefer the second option. Less insulting.
===

title: milo_discovery_first_crystal
---
Milo: Crystal. Aether-charged, by the look of it.
Milo: Don't pocket it bare-handed if you value your fingernails — actually, too late, you already did.
===

title: milo_discovery_first_lore_stone
---
Milo: Carvings. Old script. I can read about a third of it.
Milo: The rest is either prayer or shopping list. With this lot, could be either.
===

title: milo_discovery_skeleton
---
Milo: Bones. Big ones. Bigger than a man's got business being.
Milo: Don't touch the skull. Don't — right, you touched it.
===

title: milo_discovery_buried_dome
---
Milo: There. Under the silt. Tell me you feel that hum.
Milo: Whole building down there, holding its breath.
===

title: milo_discovery_pipe_organ
---
Milo: An organ. Out here. Of course there's an organ.
Milo: If you play it wrong it'll wake something. If you play it right, also something. Choose carefully.
===

title: milo_discovery_artifact_scroll
---
Milo: Vellum. Real vellum, not the printed muck.
Milo: Someone hid this and meant it to be found. Just — not by us, probably.
===

title: milo_discovery_mud_pool
---
Milo: That pool's not water. Don't drink it. Don't bathe in it. Don't look at it for too long.
Milo: I've said my piece.
===

// ============================================================
// LORE NODES — Milo speculates about Tartaria
// ============================================================

title: milo_lore_who_built
---
Milo: Who built it? Buggered if I know.
Milo: The maps call them Tartarians but the maps are wrong about most things.
Milo: Whoever they were, they built in resonance. Stone that sings. Glass that thinks.
===

title: milo_lore_the_flood
---
Milo: Mud came up overnight, the stories say. One generation, two — and the cities were gone.
Milo: I don't believe it was natural. Floods don't bury cathedrals to the spire.
===

title: milo_lore_reset_agents
---
Milo: There are people who don't want this dug up. Call themselves caretakers. They aren't.
Milo: If you see one — pale coats, hollow eyes — you run or you ring them like a bell.
===

title: milo_lore_frequency
---
Milo: Everything sings. Stone, bone, the bloody weather.
Milo: The old ones knew the notes. We're just — hearing them again. Slowly.
===

title: milo_lore_cathedrals
---
Milo: Cathedrals weren't churches. Not really. Antennae, I reckon.
Milo: Pointed at something. Listening for something. Could be God. Could be — well. Could be worse.
===

title: milo_lore_anastasia
---
Milo: You'll meet a girl. Calls herself a princess. Don't laugh.
Milo: She remembers things she shouldn't be old enough to remember. That's all I'll say.
===

title: milo_lore_the_song
---
Milo: There's a song under everything. Older than language.
Milo: I hum a few bars when I'm scared. Don't tell anyone.
===

title: milo_lore_giants
---
Milo: The bones aren't a hoax. I've measured them.
Milo: Either people used to be larger, or we used to share the world with something that pretended to be people.
Milo: Sleep on that one.
===

// ============================================================
// AMBIENT NODES — idle remarks, curious / distracted
// ============================================================

title: milo_ambient_1
---
Milo: Mud's quiet today. Suspicious.
===

title: milo_ambient_2
---
Milo: Did you hear that? No? Probably nothing. Probably.
===

title: milo_ambient_3
---
Milo: I had a hat like that once. Lost it to a goat. Long story.
===

title: milo_ambient_4
---
Milo: Wind's off the east. Smells of copper. Don't like it.
===

title: milo_ambient_5
---
Milo: Sometimes I think the buildings are watching us back.
Milo: Then I have a drink and I think it again, but louder.
===

title: milo_ambient_6
---
Milo: Blimey. Look at the light on those tiles.
===

title: milo_ambient_7
---
Milo: You ever notice the birds won't fly over the cathedral? Just — go round.
===

title: milo_ambient_8
---
Milo: I'm hungry. Ignore me. Carry on.
===

// ============================================================
// COMBAT NODES — encounter reactions
// ============================================================

title: milo_combat_mud_golem
---
Milo: Mud golem. Big lad. Hit it with a clean tone, not a loud one.
Milo: Loud just annoys it. Clean — clean unmakes it.
===

title: milo_combat_reset_scout
---
Milo: That's one of them. Reset scout. Don't let it finish that signal.
Milo: Whatever it's calling, we don't want to meet.
===

title: milo_combat_player_hit
---
Milo: Up. Get up. I'm not carrying you back, you weigh a ton and I've got a bad knee.
===

title: milo_combat_victory
---
Milo: Well struck. Bit messy at the end but — well struck.
===

// ============================================================
// CELEBRATION NODES — restoration milestones
// ============================================================

title: milo_celebration_first_restoration
---
Milo: Look at it. Look at it.
Milo: Hundred years of silence, and you just — gave it back its voice. Fancy that.
===

title: milo_celebration_cathedral_light
---
Milo: Oh. Oh, my.
Milo: The whole valley's singing. You did that. You — well I never.
Milo: Don't say anything. Just stand here a moment. With me.
===
